    <item>
      <title>19 Jul 2025 21:30</title>
      <link>https://srikanthperinkulam.com/2025/07/19/week-with-s/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Jul 2025 21:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://srikanthperinkulam.com/2025/07/19/week-with-s/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s a weird feeling. To not be presence-aware of someone 24x7.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Until now, S had either been with both M and I or just M when I travel for work. I haven&amp;rsquo;t had the chance to be with just S alone for a long stretch. Until last week. M&amp;amp;I thought it might be a good idea for her to travel with me from Dubai. It felt like she matured all of a sudden during Mummyjaan&amp;rsquo;s hospitalization. Maybe she sensed the stress all around her and adapted?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As S traveled with me, zipping across 6 cities, I felt I was constantly on the hook. How much buffer time do I need to get her ready? Did she use the bathroom before we head out? Did I keep a spare set of clothes with me? Will I find the food that she might like in the new place? If not, did I have enough snack options for her? Do I need to get her clothes washed in this city or the next? Which PJ set would she like tonight? How do I coax her to sleep despite all the flux around her? What am I forgetting?&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And to not do that, now that she isn&amp;rsquo;t with me, It feels odd. And then, when it actually dawns that M&amp;rsquo;s doing this more or less 24x7x365 - besides the gazillion other things she does; I think the least I can do is get involved a lot more.
&lt;a href=&#34;https://srikanthperinkulam.com/2025/07/19/week-with-s/&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration: none !important;&#34;&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>It&rsquo;s a weird feeling. To not be presence-aware of someone 24x7.</p>
<p>Until now, S had either been with both M and I or just M when I travel for work. I haven&rsquo;t had the chance to be with just S alone for a long stretch. Until last week. M&amp;I thought it might be a good idea for her to travel with me from Dubai. It felt like she matured all of a sudden during Mummyjaan&rsquo;s hospitalization. Maybe she sensed the stress all around her and adapted?</p>
<p>As S traveled with me, zipping across 6 cities, I felt I was constantly on the hook. How much buffer time do I need to get her ready? Did she use the bathroom before we head out? Did I keep a spare set of clothes with me? Will I find the food that she might like in the new place? If not, did I have enough snack options for her? Do I need to get her clothes washed in this city or the next? Which PJ set would she like tonight? How do I coax her to sleep despite all the flux around her? What am I forgetting?&hellip;</p>
<p>And to not do that, now that she isn&rsquo;t with me, It feels odd. And then, when it actually dawns that M&rsquo;s doing this more or less 24x7x365 - besides the gazillion other things she does; I think the least I can do is get involved a lot more.
<a href="https://srikanthperinkulam.com/2025/07/19/week-with-s/" style="text-decoration: none !important;">🔗</a>
</p>
]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    
